data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":93,"item_id":"rs_09588862fee6049c016aca05192f5081959d651436d972ca34","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Resolving onchange issues**\n\nI'm troubleshooting how the existing test interacts with the \"onchange\" event. It seems like the count could double if I use the same pattern with \"disabled\" before the name or select element. I need to make sure to avoid this pattern when the \"disabled\" attribute is in place. A solution could involve prioritizing and placing \"onchange\" before \"disabled.\" It’s a little confusing, but I want to ensure it works smoothly!"}

